# Testing

- **Runner:** `pytest`. Always invoke via `uv run pytest`.
- **No network in tests.** Use the deterministic mock LLM provider
  (`epublate.llm.mock`). Tests must pass on a freshly cloned repo
  with no API keys.
- **No flaky tests.** Tests with timing/ordering hazards must use
  `pytest-asyncio` or Textual's pilot, never `time.sleep`.

## What to test where

| Module                | Style                                         |
| --------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |
| `core/segmentation`   | `hypothesis`: `assemble(segment(doc)) == doc` |
| `core/pipeline`       | unit tests with mock LLM + fixture project    |
| `formats/epub`        | round-trip on tiny ePubs in `tests/fixtures/` |
| `glossary/enforcer`   | unit tests, every status (proposed/conf/lock) |
| `llm/openai_compat`   | unit tests with `httpx.MockTransport`         |
| `app/` (Textual)      | `pytest-textual-snapshot`                     |

## Coverage targets

- 85% line coverage on `core/`, `formats/`, `glossary/`, `llm/`,
  `db/`. UI lower bar but every screen has at least one snapshot.

## Fixtures

- ePub fixtures live in `tests/fixtures/` and must be **small** and
  **CC0-licensed**. Don't commit copyrighted books.
- Sample glossaries and prompts live in `tests/fixtures/glossary/`
  and `tests/fixtures/prompts/`.

## Don't

```python
# ❌ BAD
def test_translate():
    client = openai.OpenAI()         # real network call
    out = translate("hello", client) # non-deterministic
    assert "hola" in out.lower()

# ✅ GOOD
def test_translate(mock_llm):
    mock_llm.set_response({"target": "hola", "used_entries": []})
    out = translate_segment(seg, provider=mock_llm)
    assert out.target == "hola"
    assert mock_llm.call_count == 1
```
